I bought this to replace my 25 1/2 year old Weber Spirit, which had most of the guts replaced at least once , but the frame was rusting.
LIKES- the lid and the way it opens flush to the wall;
           -the electric starter;
           - the swing down side table.
DISLIKES- that it was made in China;
                - the gas knobs!*some of this is my fault , but read on..
 The new Spirit knobs turn counter-clockwise. in my first 3 uses i had all knobs turned fully on , and the temp never exceeded 400. Strange. Then i saw it. The 3 o'clock and final position is actually 25%! there is a small circle at that position which has a 25% piece of pie. The 9 o'clock and first position is full on. Well this is counter-intuitive. When i turn on a faucet , the more i turn the more water i get. I wrote to three friends who purchased Webers this year. TWO of them had the same complaint-- not hot enough! the third , an engineer, figured it out by the sound of the gas being released. The other two thought this low fire was a "new normal" and they now get it. and by the way , my old Spirit knobs worked clockwise, no markings - just the more you turned it , the more gas was dispensed.
I suggest Weber label the thing "HI, MED, LO" - you know , an American thing!
